						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#527">Guild rules</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							1.To become a member, the prospect must prove his worth to one of the officers of this clan. The officers of this clan will interview each prospect and decide if he/she is able to carry the Crusader name. Once that officer has found the prospect suitable by his opinion, then another member will be brought in to approve. ONLY after two members(with one officer) agree on a prospect, can that prospect be invited into the guild.<br />
<br />
2. Members of this guild will follow the chain of command stated in the officers list at all times! <br />
<br />
3. Upon acceptance, sponsors will help you learn our three main languages: dwarvish, elvish and human. It is the responsibility of the sponsor and new member to schedule a language fair with an officer. <br />
<br />
4. Guild Honor is to be upheld AT ALL TIMES. Guild honor comes before personal opinion or preference. <br />
<br />
5. Should you encounter a problem with another guild (ex:trains, kill steals, poor behavior, etc.) contact an Officer immediately. DO NOT take matters into your own hands. We stand behind all our members, but dishonorable actions will not be tolerated. <br />
<br />
6. The crusader crede is Strength and Honor! <br />
<br />
7. There is to be no selling among brothers. We give freely. Trading is accepted but not encouraged. The goal is to give and receive without obligation so that all may grow equally. If an item has been listed in guildsay for three days and no members want the item, it can be sold by the owner at his/her convenience.<br />
<br />
8. We are not a clan in search of items and experience ONLY. We exist to provide companionship with our fellow brothers. We are not here to simply gain items or experience. We are a family. <br />
<br />
9. Fairplay and manners are always expected. This is a roleplaying server - roleplaying behavior is preferred (ie: language and actions). <br />
<br />
10. We, as a clan, oppose ALL that is evil in Norrath. Grouping with evil characters is ok as long as it is only for a short enough time to get what you are after.<br />
<br />
11. Our clan has several allies. Refer to the guild history to see a listing. Our allies are to be treated as one of our own. Buff them, heal them, assist them in any way whenever you see them. <br />
<br />
12. Any faultering from the above rules will result in disciplinary action. Disciplinary actions, dependent upon incident are: meeting with an officer, public apology, duels to the death in arena, day of servitude, banishment from the clan.
